    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Karen G.",
        "date": "2025-06-24T20:10:08Z",
        "id": "685b144d1c206e784bb30603",
        "label": "Okay",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 6,
        "responses": [
          {
            "date": "Jul 8, 2025",
            "id": "09922a38-b78b-4d89-a92a-24e062fdae78",
            "locale": "en_ca",
            "response": "Thank you for taking the time to share your feedback, Karen. We sincerely apologize for the mix-up regarding the sheet delivery. It was certainly not the experience we intended to provide, and we regret the inconvenience it caused during your stay.\n\nWe appreciate you bringing the other maintenance concerns to our attention. While the home does make a strong first impression, we understand how the issues you encountered may have affected your comfort. We are actively working with our team to address these matters so that future guests may enjoy a more seamless experience.\n\nWe were glad to promptly reimburse you for the sheets and also issued a partial refund of the cleaning fee along with applicable taxes. Additionally, we have extended a 5% discount on a future stay at any of our qualified homes, and we hope you will give us another opportunity to host you again.\n\nIt is wonderful to hear that you enjoyed the layout of the home and the convenience of each room having its own bathroom. We also appreciate your helpful notes about the beach access and parking, which will certainly benefit future guests.\n\nThank you once again for your thoughtful comments. We value your input and are committed to making necessary improvements.\n\nWarm regards, Benchmark Management",
            "user": "VrboOwner"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Upon initial arrival, the property makes a great impression. Most of the issues we experienced related to the construction of the house. Interior doors won't close, windows wouldn't lock, microwave was only partially installed, toilet flushed slow, light bulbs flickered, etc. ... We did have an issue with dirty sheets in the primary. I requested new sheets and the wrong size was delivered. In the end, we bought our own and the management company reimbursed us without issue. The home is not as fully stocked as other beach homes we've stayed in. It was fairly close to the beach. Some of us road bikes to the beach using the underground tunnel under the main road. There is parking at Inlet beach but it is limited if you arrive after 9:00 AM. We loved that every room had its' own bathroom. The house has much potential but needs more attention.",
        "themes": [
          "Liked: Cleanliness, check-in, location"
        ],
        "title": "Could have been better",
        "verified": true
      },
      {
        "author": "Deirdre P.",
        "date": "2025-07-31T22:43:51Z",
        "id": "688c0056ede6a2656ec0f428",
        "label": "Poor",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 4,
        "responses": [
          {
            "date": "Sep 11, 2025",
            "id": "758243c8-321b-42cb-9dcc-598f466af053",
            "locale": "en_us",
            "response": "We’re so sorry to hear that your stay at 28 Queen Palm was not the peaceful vacation you had hoped for. We know how special these trips are for families, and it’s disappointing that maintenance and inspection issues disrupted your time with us.\n\nWe appreciate the grace you showed our technicians, and we also recognize how frustrating it must have been to experience recurring problems. To acknowledge this, we have provided a refund along a discount towards a future booking with us.\n\nPlease know that your comments will be used to improve how we manage and inspect our homes so that future guests enjoy a seamless experience. We would love the chance to welcome you back under much better circumstances.",
            "user": "VrboOwner"
          }
        ],
        "text": "I recommend the home at 28 Queen Palm once repairs are made. While staying there my family and I experienced insects on the patio to the point where we could not use any patio and leaks in the home. We couldn’t use the plumbing in some spaces of the home. Though the service techs were nice we had three visits for repairs during our three night stay. Which was beyond ridiculous and a bit intrusive! While vacating the home we found mold like substance in the garage! The WORST part of this whole ordeal is Benchmark Management! They’ve done a poor job at managing the home and caring for customer’s inconvenience. I have had to follow up nonstop and they refuse to properly compensate for the lackluster stay which ruined what was supposed to be a peaceful vacation. These issues could have been easily repaired if they cared to properly inspect the home for the future renters. I should have listened to the reviews as you can easily spot in the wording that there were issues from previous renters and the previous renters gave grace. Learn from feedback Benchmark.",
        "themes": [
          "Liked: Cleanliness, check-in, location",
          "Disliked: Communication, listing accuracy"
        ],
        "title": "Luxury home, but subpar management!",
        "verified": true
      },
      {
        "author": "Hmong V.",
        "date": "2025-06-13T23:02:00Z",
        "id": "68557a3a42d00a79db4bb244",
        "label": "Good",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 8,
        "text": "We had some issues at the start of our stay but management was very responsive to address and communication for our stay was great.",
        "themes": [
          "Liked: Cleanliness, check-in, communication, location, listing accuracy"
        ],
        "verified": true
      }
    ],
